        <h2 id="profiles">The 10 Jogger Pants Manufacturer Types in China (Detailed Profiles)</h2>

        <h3>1. Large Integrated Sportswear Group (Fujian)</h3>

        <p>Fujian hosts several of China's largest sportswear groups, the kind that supply global athletic brands and run their own knitting mills, dye houses, and finishing lines. If your jogger program needs bonded seams, four-way stretch, or a custom moisture-wicking finish at volume, start here</p>

        <p><strong>Core Strengths</strong></p>

        <ul class="ar-list"><li>Vertically integrated knit fabric production, from yarn to finished garment</li><li>Technical joggers: four-way stretch, moisture management, anti-odor treatments</li><li>In-house labs for colorfastness, shrinkage, and stretch recovery testing</li></ul>

        <p><strong>Key Facts</strong></p>

        <ul class="ar-list"><li>Typical MOQ: 1,000–3,000 pcs per style, higher when fabric is developed from scratch</li><li>Lead time: sampling 10–20 days, bulk 45–75 days, plus 25–35 days sea freight</li><li>Certifications commonly held: BSCI, WRAP, ISO 9001</li><li>Main markets: US, EU, Japan</li></ul>

        <p>This tier makes sense when you are running 10,000+ units and need fabric R&amp;D you can absorb into a longer development cycle</p>

        <h3>2. Knitwear Specialist (Guangdong)</h3>

        <p>The Dongguan and Foshan knitwear cluster built its name on French terry and loopback fleece bottoms. These factories keep tight sample rooms and know jogger construction cold: ribbed cuffs, flat drawcords, side-seam pockets, and the stitch density that stops a cuff from going slack by the tenth wash. Garment dyeing and enzyme wash for vintage finishes are standard in-house services here, and first protos usually land in 7–12 days</p>

        <p><strong>Key Facts</strong></p>

        <ul class="ar-list"><li>Typical MOQ: 300–800 pcs per color</li><li>Lead time: bulk 30–50 days after sample approval, plus 20–30 days shipping</li><li>Certifications commonly held: BSCI, OEKO-TEX</li><li>Fabric range: French terry and loopback fleece, 240–400 GSM</li><li>Main markets: EU, Australia</li></ul>

        <p>Mid-size brands and streetwear labels chasing washed or garment-dyed finishes fit this tier without stepping into a tier-one factory's MOQ</p>

        <h3>3. Streetwear-Focused Factory (Guangdong)</h3>

        <p>A subset of Guangdong plants deliberately target streetwear and DTC brands. They handle 400–500 GSM fleece, oversized blocks, and short color runs. The tradeoff is ceiling capacity: these shops are engineered for flexibility, not for 100,000-piece programs</p>

